  "description": "With its newly re-designed frame, the PD 2 features a low stand-over height for easier climbing in & out of the saddle. Its lightweight aluminum frame features an internal head tube, internal cable routing and an improved kickstand position. It comes standard with a 2x9 drive train, versatile and capable of handling a wide variety of terrain. It rolls along on strong double-wall rims, stainless spokes and Kenda Kwick Seven.5 tires with reflective sidewalls for increased safety. The PD2 model features a Suntour XCT-30 100mm travel fork with a hydraulic lockout, which deactivates the up and down motion associated with suspension. The PD2 model is your trusted partner for community and outreach patrols.\nNew Haro PD2 27.5\" X6 frame, updated kickstand position\nSuntour XCT-30 HLO fork, 100mm\nAltus MT210-2 36/22T crankset\nAlivio M4000 2x9 derailleurs\nPivit Adjustable-rise stem, ext.: 105mm\nComfort grips w/ integrated Bar-Ends\nWTB Comfort Sport saddle\nMX-21 27.5\" Aluminum DW rims w/ Stainless spokes\nKenda Kwick Seven 2.0\" tires w/ reflective stripes\nPromax disc brakes w/ 160mm rotors\nRear rack, water-bottle cage & kickstand",
